# Expertise consultations

Canonical detail lives in **`AGENTS.md` → section "Expertise consultations"**. Keep that section accurate when behavior changes.

## Invariants

- Tag `expertise` is a fourth inventory category (`/expertise`, filter, Add Item). The list uses the same grid as the other categories (3 per row from 900px): photo, name, and **short text** (`body`, max 180). Opening an expert shows **long text** (`long_body` / `longBody`, max 4000, migration `007_expertise_copy.sql`) in a narrow overlay. Until `longBody` is set, a blank line in `body` splits list text (first paragraph) from the overlay bio. Cards say **Request Consultation** and hide availability badges. `longBody` is public; `expert_email` is not.
- Consultations **reuse** `reservations` + `POST /api/inventory/:id/reservations` — not a separate table.
- Create body: `{ timeSlots, summary }` (not dates). Server sets start/end to submission date. **No date collision** for expertise, but a member gets **one open request per expert**: a pending or not-yet-held consultation on the same item → 409 `consultation_already_open` (checked in `addReservation` inside the item lock).
- Reservation create has two limiters: the IP limiter **before** `requireAuth` (it shields Supabase auth), then `reservationAccountLimiter` **after** it (10 saved creates per account per 24 h, keyed by user id, 429 `daily_request_limit`; `countSavedReservationCreates()` refunds a create that saved nothing, and a saved one counts even if the client disconnects). In-memory: single Cloud Run instance only. Every 429 from this route carries a `code` (`reservation_rate_limited`, `daily_request_limit`, `pending_request_limit`) mapped in `ERROR_CODE_KEYS`, so the form and calendar show it in EN/FR; keep it that way for any new limit.
- UI: `ConsultationRequestForm.svelte` replaces `ItemCalendar` in the expertise overlay (compact panel, not the three-column calendar layout). It asks for up to three **Date** / **From** / **To** times and/or the member's own words and joins them into the one `timeSlots` string (a line per time in the member's language and device time zone, then the words; max 500), so the API body and every place that echoes `time_slots` stay as they are.
- **The expert** is the signed-in user whose **confirmed** email matches the item's `expert_email` (case-insensitive). Experts schedule, move, follow up and cancel from the `/account` agenda (`AccountAgenda.svelte`, `AgendaConsultationCard.svelte`); admins can do the same from `/admin` (moving: API only). **Owners (migration 015):** every item has `owner_email`; the effective host is `itemOwnerEmail(item)` = `expert_email` when set, else `owner_email`. A confirmed owner of a mentor with no `expert_email` is `isOwner` in `loadConsultationForUser`, sees its consultations in `asExpert`, and may do everything the expert does. Emails word what a host did with `consultationHostVoice()` (`'expert'` for the mentor and a non-staff owner, `'admin'` for staff); never decide that from `isExpert` alone. `owner_email` / `ownerEmail` never reaches a public or `/account` payload. On the agenda, pending requests and upcoming meetings show under **Needs you** (requests the mentor or owner must schedule), **Coming up** (the member's requests under **Sent, waiting for a reply**, then scheduled meetings on the timeline) and, for one visit, **Changed since your last visit**. Cancelled, declined, and finished meetings (60 minutes after the start) go to the collapsed **Earlier** section. Every question before an action, there and on `/admin`, is an `InlineConfirm` with the action's `*_confirm` text, never `window.confirm`.
- **Share Expertise** (`AccountShareExpertise.svelte`) is on every account, behind a button on the account panel. The form stays closed until that button is clicked. A confirmed member can publish **one** mentor profile (`POST /api/account/mentor-profile`). `expert_email` is forced to the JWT email. The profile is an expertise item and shows on the Expertise list. `PATCH` edits it only when that email matches; it does not change the email or the slug. If several items share the email, the earliest is the one they edit.
- Lifecycle: `pending` → `reserved` (scheduled, `meeting_at` + Zoom fields) → `cancelled`; or `pending` → `refused` (admin) / `cancelled`. A **follow-up** (`POST /api/consultations/:id/follow-up`, expert, owner or admin, `bookFollowUpConsultation`) is a new row created straight as `reserved` with a Zoom meeting and `follow_up_of` = the source; the source must be `reserved` with its meeting's **Montréal date today or earlier** (`libraryTodayKey`, so from the morning of the meeting, not from its start), the follow-up must start after the source meeting (400 `follow_up_before_meeting`), and the one-open-request rule applies (ignoring the source). Members can't book follow-ups; experts do it from `/account`, admins from `/admin` → Edit Reservations, and both lists decide where the button shows with `canBookFollowUp()` (`reservation-rules.js`). **Staff bookings:** `/admin` → **Create Reservation** on a mentor (`POST /api/admin/inventory/:id/reservations { email, meetingAt, summary?, message? }`, `addReservation` with `meetingAt` and the Zoom callbacks) also creates a row straight as `reserved`, for any address, member or not, with a Zoom meeting made in the item lock and `booked_by_staff`; the one-open-request rule applies (409 `reservation_consultation_open`, checked before Zoom) and a Zoom failure saves nothing (502). Only schedule, move (reschedule), follow-up, cancel, refuse, and admin delete change consultations; the admin reservation `PATCH` returns 400 for expertise items.
- **Held** = `reserved` with `meetingAt` + 60 min ≤ now. There is no `completed` status; use `isConsultationHeld()` from `src/lib/reservation-rules.js` everywhere (server, store, the `/account` agenda through `src/lib/consultation-notices.js`, `AdminPanel`) instead of re-deriving it.
- Scheduling (expert `POST /api/consultations/:id/schedule` or admin approve) creates the Zoom meeting **inside the item lock** before writing `reserved`. Zoom failure → 502, nothing saved. Zoom unset → schedules without a link.
- **Moving** (`POST /api/consultations/:id/reschedule`, expert, owner or admin; `rescheduleConsultation`) only applies to a `reserved` meeting that hasn't started. It moves the Zoom meeting **inside the item lock** before writing `meeting_at` (`PATCH /meetings/{id}`, same link; a Zoom 404 or no meeting → a new meeting whose fields are saved, deleted again if the write fails). Zoom failure → 502 `consultation_zoom_failed`, nothing saved, no email. A move must keep every follow-up after the meeting it follows, both ways (400 `follow_up_before_meeting`). Both people get "Consultation moved" with an `.ics` REQUEST for the same UID.
- `.ics` `SEQUENCE` is seconds since 1970 at build time (nothing stores a revision), so the latest invite or cancel for a UID wins. Don't go back to a fixed 0/1.
- After any confirm or move, call `setReminderState(id, reservationStartsAt(…))` and then `restoreReminderIfNotEmailed` (a booking less than a day away is `skipped` because that email is its reminder, unless the email failed). The reminder pass sends consultations' "coming up" emails to both people about a day before (no `.ics`).
- Cancelling (member, expert, owner or admin; an owner is recorded as `expert` or `admin` by `consultationHostVoice()`) sets `cancelled` + `cancelled_by`, deletes the Zoom meeting (best effort, logged), and emails both member and expert. Admin delete of an active consultation (or its item) does the same. A **held** meeting is never cancelled: the cancel route returns 400 `consultation_already_held`, and admin deletes remove it as a record only (no Zoom delete, no emails). Removing an expertise item deletes all its consultation rows (FK cascade), so the admin confirm warns with the count. The cancel route returns `{ consultation, emailSent, otherPartyEmailed }`; `otherPartyEmailed` is a boolean (`emailSent` and the other side has an address on file: the mentor's for a member cancel, the member's for anyone cancelling for the mentor, an owner or admin included), never an address. The client may say "{title} has been told" to a member only when `otherPartyEmailed === true` (a mentor may have no email).
- `normalizeReservationStatus` defaults unknown statuses to `reserved` — any new status **must** be added to `RESERVATION_STATUSES` in `calendar.js`.
- `expert_email` is optional on items; **never** returned on public inventory APIs. The account mentor-profile response includes it for the signed-in owner only. Admin **Mentors** (`MentorBrowser.svelte`) edits it, plus name, short text, long text, and photo, via `PATCH /api/inventory/:id`. The slug stays as created. Blank email clears `expert_email`. Consultations follow the item, so a new address takes them over; the save emails it the expert emails it missed for each pending request and meeting not yet held (`sendMentorEmailHandover`, response `handover`, `docs/automated-emails.md` trigger 11). An account's own email change moves its mentor item and reservations through the `auth.users` trigger in `014_account_email_change.sql`.
- Public sanitization strips `timeSlots`, `requestSummary`, `meetingAt`, `userEmail`, and all Zoom/cancel fields (whitelist in `sanitizeReservationForPublic`).
- Account API: members see the expert email; experts (and owners) see the member email; neither sees other users' requests. Messages from `/account` (`POST /api/reservations/:id/message`, read with `GET /api/reservations/:id/messages?as=`) are kept in the booking's conversation (migration 016, `src/lib/reservation-messages-store.js`) and email the other side (member → `itemOwnerEmail(item)`, else `CONTACT_TO`; host → member) only when they've read the conversation since the last such email, with the library's `Reply-To` (never the sender's: no address passes between them through a message); only the booking's member (`as: 'member'`) or a confirmed `isItemOwner` (`as: 'owner'`) may read or send, everyone else gets the 404 of a missing booking.
- Emails: request-received (member) + new-request (expert) on create; scheduled (both, with Zoom link + `.ics` REQUEST; a follow-up uses the same emails worded "Follow-up consultation" with the note; a staff booking passes `account` so the member's says the library team booked it, shows the topic and invites them to log in or register with that address); cancelled (both, `.ics` CANCEL when it had been scheduled); moved (both, `.ics` REQUEST); day-before reminder (both, no `.ics`); messages (one person, Reply-To the sender); admin refuse (member only).
- The consultation form must say who receives the request: the named expert (item title) and the Apathy is Boring team, plus the member's account email (`consultation.intro`, and `consultation.sharing_note` in the **Who sees this** strip right above **Send request**). Don't use an "us" voice there.
- Zoom meetings: join before host, `jbh_time: 0`, no waiting room. "Everyone can share screen" is a **host-user setting** — set once per process via `PATCH /users/{host}/settings` (needs `user:update:settings:admin` scope) or in the Zoom web portal.
- Slack payload always includes `time_slots`, `request_summary`, `expert_email`, `admin_url` (empty strings when N/A). Slack fires on reservation create and, as staff alerts (`notifySlackAlert`), on mentor profile publish / changed edit (`status` `mentor_profile_published` / `mentor_profile_updated`) and follow-up booking (`consultation_follow_up`), with a sentence in `request_summary`. Alerts must send **exactly** the reservation keys so the workflow trigger accepts them. Every post includes `message`, the full Slack text built by the server (`reservationSlackMessage()` / `notifySlackAlert()`); the workflow message is just `{message}`, so wording changes happen in `server.js`.
- Kimchi on `/account` (`AccountAgenda.svelte`, with the rules in `src/lib/consultation-notices.js`; the action bubbles in `AgendaConsultationCard.svelte`): bubbles never contain a Zoom link, a member's email, time slots or a summary; what Kimchi remembers (`src/lib/kimchi-memory.js`) is ids, statuses and dates only. At most one load-time bubble per visit (meeting soon or live > closed by the other side > new requests > a request waiting a week), and no bubble or status line claims an email when the response has `emailSent === false`. Each bubble's news also reaches the page while Kimchi sleeps (the agenda's hidden status line, the meeting's **Starts in N min** / **Happening now** sticker, the **Changed since your last visit** section).
- Replace `CONSULTATION_DATA_FORM_URL` in `server.js` before launch.
- Migrations: `005_expertise.sql`, then `006_consultation_scheduling.sql`, then `007_expertise_copy.sql`, then `008_consultation_follow_up.sql` (`reservations.follow_up_of`). `014_account_email_change.sql` (trigger, no columns) can go in any time. `015_item_owners_and_reminders.sql` (`owner_email`, `reminder_email`, 014's function plus `owner_email`) goes after 014; re-run it if 014 is applied later.

## Locale domains

`consultation.*`, `account_consultations.*`, `account_agenda.*` (the `/account` agenda: sections, stickers, **More**, **Keep it**, the withdraw and decline questions), `share_expertise.*`, `inventory.filter_expertise`, `inventory.request_consultation`, `calendar.daily_limit`, `admin.consultation_*` / `meeting_*` / `mentors_*` / `create_consultation_*` / `create_reservation_*` (mentor meetings in Create Reservation) / `remove_expertise_confirm` / `delete_held_consultation_confirm` / `*_no_expert_email` / `no_mentor_email`, `add_item.expert_*`, `kimchi.consultation_*` (sent, scheduled, rescheduled, refused, withdrawn, cancelled by role, closed, declined, deleted, still waiting) / `message_sent` / `time_suggestion_sent` / `follow_up_booked*` / `expert_requests_waiting_*` / `meeting_starting_soon` / `meeting_live` / `mentor_updated` / `mentor_updated_handover` / `mentor_removed_notified` / `mentor_profile_published` / `mentor_profile_updated`, `seo.category_expertise_*`, `how_this_works.*` (browse/reserve/pickup + FAQ), `reservation_message.*` (the message panels, shared with rooms, equipment and books).
